# env
#
# The whole env-file FAMILY, not three shapes of it. Measured at c6de1d7:
# `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.*.local` were ignored while `.env.production`
# and `.env.staging` were NOT — so the two names a deploy-shaped file is most
# likely to take were exactly the two that staged silently, with no warning:
#
#   $ printf 'GITHUB_FINE_GRAINED_PAT=github_pat_…\n' > .env.production
#   $ git add --dry-run .env.production   ->  add '.env.production'
#
# `.env*` covers .env, .env.local, .env.production, .env.staging,
# .env.development.local and .env.production.local. `.env.example` is RE-
# ADDED below: it is the file that documents GITHUB_FINE_GRAINED_PAT for the
# operator, and it must never hold a real value, so it stays tracked as the
# example and is policed for emptiness by `bun run secrets:scan`.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env*.example

# local key material, in case an operator writes one next to the app
*.key

